      "note": "Provisional machine alignment by Codex, English-first proposal; no human or semantic approval. The first three-part clause supplies lexical parts, three, with and came; the second cha shas gsum ldan du is distributed in they stay with the glass of water and is omitted, not nulled. mthar ma zhig gi bar du is a complete temporal phrase whose negative boundary is recast as until it eventually ends. chu/phor pa select the third water/glass, the wet-and-flowing material, not earlier supplied referents. The one byas pa selects the second provides, after craving spirit, while its shared predication also licenses the earlier English provides. rnag khrag is blood and pus with reversed, strictly smaller lexical members. Other pronominal, case and connective contributions remain omitted where distributed."
